+<h2>The SOCIAL level raise is confirmed before a token or a success answer, and the rehash log says whether it landed &mdash; KS-1460, auth, TIER 1</h2>
+<div class="note"><table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What to know.</strong></td><td> A social sign-in (<code>GET /api/auth/social/:provider/callback</code>) or <code>POST /api/auth/social/link</code> that raises a BASIC account to SOCIAL and cannot confirm the database write now answers <strong>503</strong> <code>{"success":false,"error":{"code":"SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE","message":"Social sign-in could not be confirmed. Please retry — if you already succeeded, you may not need to."}}</code> (the link says "Linking the social account ..."): retry. No token or session is issued in that case. On the password login, the log line "UPGRADE-ON-VERIFY: rehashed bcrypt -&gt; argon2id" now appears only when the rehash was stored; otherwise you see the warn "the rehash write did not take effect (non-fatal); the old hash stays", and the login still succeeds.
+    </td></tr><tr><td><strong>Behaviour change:</strong> before, both social routes answered success (and the callback minted a SOCIAL token) even when the level was never stored. Still open: <code>POST /social/link</code>'s social-id write is not persisted at all (KS-1672), so its "linked" answer is not yet true. Test files: <code>services/auth/src/__tests__/ks1460-social-level-raise-confirms-the-write.test.ts</code> and <code>ks1460-rehash-log-is-truthful.test.ts</code>.
+    </td></tr></table></div>
