+<h2><!--n-->. The SOCIAL level raise is confirmed before a token or a success answer, and the rehash log says whether it landed (KS-1460, auth, TIER 1)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> Before, three login-path writes in <code>services/auth/src/routes/auth.ts</code> discarded <code>userRepo.updateUser</code>'s answer, which is <code>null</code> when the UPDATE matched no row. The social sign-in callback (<code>GET /api/auth/social/:provider/callback</code>) raised a BASIC account to <code>verificationLevel: 'SOCIAL'</code>, set the in-memory copy to SOCIAL and minted a token pair over that unconfirmed write. <code>POST /api/auth/social/link</code> did the same raise and answered <code>success: true</code>. The password login's UPGRADE-ON-VERIFY rehash logged "rehashed bcrypt -&gt; argon2id" whether or not the write landed.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Now both SOCIAL raises call <code>updateUserOrThrow</code>: a write that did not land answers <strong>503</strong> <code>SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE</code> ("Social sign-in could not be confirmed. Please retry" / "Linking the social account could not be confirmed. Please retry"), with no session, no token and no success answer. The rehash logs its info line only when the write landed, and a warn "the rehash write did not take effect (non-fatal); the old hash stays" otherwise. The login is unchanged either way.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Unchanged, by Wednesday's ruling of 2026-11-05: the <code>lastLoginAt</code> write (best effort; <code>updateUser</code> already warns on 0 rows) and the two social-id link writes. Those belong to KS-1672: <code>updateUser</code> drops social-id fields, so there is no failure for <code>updateUserOrThrow</code> to catch, and <code>POST /social/link</code>'s "linked" answer stays false until that ticket lands.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.1 Evidence</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="3"><strong>How it was tested.</strong></td><td> Two new files in <code>services/auth/src/__tests__/</code>. <code>ks1460-social-level-raise-confirms-the-write.test.ts</code> has 6 cells on the ks795 harness. Its repository double models the real contract: <code>updateUser</code> answers null for a write that did not land, and <code>updateUserOrThrow</code> is <code>updateUser</code> plus a 503 on null. <code>ks1460-rehash-log-is-truthful.test.ts</code> has 2 cells on the ks1868 login harness. On develop <code>5fc5569ed96a</code>: 2 of 6 and 1 of 2 failed, every one by assertion (200 with a minted token, 200 <code>linked: true</code>, and the "rehashed" line logged over a write that did not land); every control passed. With the change: 6 of 6 and 2 of 2.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>Seven mutants, all admissible (tsc rc 0), all killed by assertion: either route back to the discarding <code>updateUser</code>; either throw swallowed with <code>.catch(() =&gt; null)</code>; the info line logged always; the branches swapped; the warn dropped.
+    </td></tr><tr><td>The social and login harnesses (ks795, ks728, ks722, ks1240b, ks1858, ks1885, ks1868-auth, ks781, ks1157, ks1967 and others): 33 of 33 files, 423 of 423 tests. ks795 needed <code>updateUserOrThrow</code> added to its repository mock; it records into the same list and lands, and no assertion changed. Whole auth suite: 1,693 of 1,695 with the change. The 2 are <code>ks949-platform-admin-seed-identity</code> timeouts under load, the same cells that timed out on develop. <code>tsc --noEmit</code> rc 0; eslint clean; test-file type ratchet 0 new (41 in the baseline).
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3><!--n-->.2 What it does not cover</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="1"><strong>Not measured here.</strong></td><td> A real database 0-row UPDATE (fail-closed RLS with an unresolved tenant GUC is the case that produces one), a booted auth service, a real social provider, the four platform suites, KS-1672's social-id persistence, Node 24 (host Node v26.8.1, not an LTS line).
+    </td></tr></table>
